    ["观众的视线永远注视着别人，从不曾留下自己的痕迹，这是馈赠，也是诅咒。你可以尽情阅读无数人的故事，可以欢呼，可以流泪，但永远要记得保持旁观，而非参与其中。\n“为什么？我就不能成为故事的主人公，去改变命运吗？”\n某位观众提出疑问，她不忍心看着故事走向既定的悲剧，总忍不住去注解一个好结局，因此她的魔药消化进度近乎停滞，终于有一天，她陷入了失控的命运。\n“谁会来看我的故事……谁会……写下我的结局……”\n回答她的，是一只充满哀悼的眼睛。"] = "The Spectator's gaze is always fixed on others, never leaving a trace of themselves. This is a gift, and also a curse. You can read the stories of countless people to your heart's content, you can cheer, and you can weep, but you must always remember to remain an observer, not a participant. \n \"Why? Can't I become the protagonist of the story and change fate?\" \n A certain Spectator raised this question. She could not bear to watch the story head toward a predetermined tragedy and could not help but annotate a good ending. Consequently, her potion digestion progress nearly stalled, and finally, one day, she fell into a fate of loss of control. \n \"Who will watch my story... who will... write my ending...\" \n Answering her was an eye filled with mourning.",
